<div id="2026-11-12-healthkitchen-meal-slots" class="cl-entry">
<h3>2026-11-12 — Health Kitchen: meal slots, slot logging and recipe setup</h3>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>What.</strong> The day's meal slots are now a first-class surface. <code>/healthkitchen/slots</code> shows the user's slots with the recipe behind each one and its ingredients; <code>slot_log</code>, <code>drink_out</code>, <code>meal_out</code> and <code>setup_apply</code> are POST-only actions that record intake, an out-and-about drink, a described meal, and the one-time "morning beverage + coffee" setup. Slot definitions live in the user preference <code>healthkitchen.meal_slots</code> (<code>{ sitename => [ slot ] }</code>), validated by <code>MealSlots->valid_pref</code>. The Todo day cards read the same slots so a scheduled plate shows its recipe and an in-place "Mark made" button after Done; that read derives display data and persists nothing. Intake rows gained <code>kind</code>, <code>slot_key</code>, <code>recipe_id</code>, <code>meal_plan_entry_id</code>, <code>started_at</code>, <code>ended_at</code>, <code>duration_min</code>, <code>source</code>, <code>location</code> and <code>description</code>.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Why.</strong> A day of eating was only expressible as a free-text note. Slot logging has to name the recipe that was made, keep the user's wall clock for start and end, and distinguish planned food from food eaten out without inventing a second diary.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Files.</strong> <code>lib/Comserv/Util/HealthKitchen/{MealSlots,MealLog,SlotRecipe,RecipeSetup,Backup}.pm</code>, <code>lib/Comserv/Controller/HealthKitchen.pm</code>, <code>lib/Comserv/Controller/Todo.pm</code>, <code>lib/Comserv/Util/UserPreferences.pm</code>, <code>lib/Comserv/Model/Schema/Ency/Result/HealthKitchen/IntakeLog.pm</code>, <code>root/healthkitchen/{slots,_meal_slots,index,recipes}.tt</code>, <code>root/todo/{day,todo_card}.tt</code>, <code>root/static/js/healthkitchen/recipe-confirm.js</code>. Needs schema-compare: the ten <code>hk_intake_log</code> columns above.</p>
</div>
